--- !u!114 &145303242
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 145303241}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e99934f89aae5704f9c283809cf4edcd, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::MusicProgram.CrestURP.CrestURPShowcaseNotes
  controls: 'DESKTOP: WASD move, Q/E descend/ascend, Shift sprint, hold RMB to look.

    VR:
    OpenXR headset drives the Main Camera; move the XR Origin to cross the surface.


    VALIDATION:
    start above water, lower through Y=0, inspect the meniscus, then look at the
    seafloor/rocks for projected caustics. The player, floating bodies, surface submarine
    and fish school inject forces into Crest Dynamic Waves. Planar reflections render
    above water. Caustics use Snell-refraction ray differentials and the live surface-to-receiver
    Jacobian, with no procedural caustic pattern. Use CrestURPWaveController for
    presets, runtime time control, Dynamic Waves, foam, and detailed 14-band spectrum
    authoring. Floating bodies use Crest GPU displacement queries. Ocean LOD, FFT
    waves and foam are generated by the MIT Crest Water 4 core.'
